[[Custodian stalker]]s can be assigned as a [[Slayer task]] starting at level 54 by [[Chaeldar]], [[Nieve]], and [[Mortimer]], and can be found in the [[Stalker Den]] after the completion of the [[Shadows of Custodia]] [[quest]]. There are [[multicombat]] areas where [[Dwarf multicannon|cannons]] can be placed in the south-western side of the dungeon, and single-combat caverns in the south-eastern and northern parts.

The stalkers all drop [[broken antler]]s, which are used to create [[atlatl dart tips]] for creating [[atlatl dart]]s outside of subduing the [[Moons of Peril]]. The [[Mature custodian stalker|mature]] and [[Elder custodian stalker|elder]] variants are also able to drop the [[antler guard]], a powerful off-hand item boasting offensive stats in all styles, with no defence requirement to wield. These tougher variants require a higher Slayer level to fight however, of level 67 and 76 respectively.

While most damage can be prevented with the use of [[Protect from Melee]], once their Hitpoints get low they will use a special attack that causes a [[bleed]] effect; this attack can be blocked with [[Protect from Magic]]. When fighting multiple at once, changing prayers can be unwise, so some healing may be necessary. Gear with high magic defence such as [[dragonhide armour]] can be beneficial to reduce the amount of damage taken. [[Bones to Peaches]] can also allow the player to sustain longer trips with only prayer gear and potions. Stalkers also drop cooked fish, which may be enough to keep up with damage.

Players who wish to do this task are encouraged to get 76 Slayer in order to kill the [[Elder custodian stalker|elder stalkers]]. In addition to better drops, only the elders can spawn a [[superior slayer monster]], the [[Ancient Custodian]].

